# DAMIC-M DM-electron limit (arXiv:2503.14617, 90% CL, heavy mediator F_DM = 1, QCDark1 + analytic MTF
# screening) rescaled to the RAPIDD silicon response (QCDark2 RPA dielectric function with local field
# effects, arXiv:2603.12326): sigma_e = DAMIC-M_2025_DMe_heavy_QCDark.dat x S_DAMIC-M/S_RAPIDD, with
# S = sum_{Q=2..4} eps_Q R_Q (eps_Q = 0.38, 0.65, 0.79 pattern efficiencies), Ramanathan-Kurinsky 100 K
# charge yield and the same halo (SHM of arXiv:2105.00599) for both. S_DAMIC-M reimplements the QCDark1
# rate with its published Si form factor (github.com/asingal14/QCDark efdb7d1, results/Si_final.hdf5).
# Approximate: charge diffusion, pattern details, backgrounds and Earth shielding are not modelled.
# Masses with (1/2) m (v_esc + v_E)^2 below the Q = 4 onset (6.75 eV, m < 1.9 MeV) are omitted: there the
# signal comes from the kinematic end point and the ratio is not reliable.
# Written by examples/damicm_dme_limit_rapidd.py.
# DM mass [GeV]   sigma_e [cm^2]   S_RAPIDD/S_DAMIC-M   S_QCDark2-MTF/S_DAMIC-M (diagnostic)
